[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:She Was Not Amused]
[00:13.81]Why did Jenny want to leave the wedding reception?
[00:19.73]Jeremy Hampden has a large circle of friends and is very popular at parties.
[00:26.78]Everybody admires him for his great sense of humour--everybody, that is, except his six-year-old daughter, Jenny.
[00:37.58]Recently, one of Jeremy's closest friends asked him to make a speech at a wedding reception.
[00:45.52]This is the sort of thing that Jeremy loves.
[00:49.55]He prepared the speech carefully and
[00:52.67]went to the wedding with Jenny.
[00:55.59]He had included a large number of funny stories in the speech and,
[01:00.30]of course, it was a great success.
[01:03.79]As soon as he had finished
[01:06.19]Jenny told him she wanted to go home.
[01:10.36]Jeremy was a little disappointed by this
[01:13.67]but he did as his daughter asked.
[01:16.72]On the way home, he asked Jenny if she had enjoyed the speech.
[01:22.95]To his surprise she said she hadn't.
[01:27.72]Jeremy asked her why this was so and she told him that she did not like to
[01:34.17]see so many people laughing at him!
